{"kind":"request","text":"C3 rule 5 can select an earlier live signing, but C1 send always sends the latest. Example: key k signs values A, is refused at a head; signs values B, is refused; the member submits A again at the same expected revisions while the first signing lives. Section 4 rule 5 says to resend A's exact bytes. Custody.send reads record.envelope (latest B), and its outcome always uses signings.length - 1. A callback that substitutes A would falsely attribute its outcome to B, so I will not do that.\n\nProposal: extend Custody.send with a selected signing index for resubmission and retain that selected index as the current attempt's signing in the v2 record. The top-level envelope stays the latest-created signing, as section 5.1 requires. C3's current present values and retry schedule read the selected signing for the current attempt, with v2 records lacking the field defaulting to their latest signing. A new signing selects itself; a resend of an earlier signing selects it before dispatch under the same lock. The client changes no wire shape. The v2 store shape gains one optional field.\n\nAlternative: constrain rule 5 to the latest live signing, and sign A again when it equals only an earlier signing. That needs a design amendment and spends another signing. Which behavior does C3 build?","body":{"conditions":"Rule on an earlier live signing that equals the newly built intent before C3 changes Custody's send selection.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}